# Cursor AI Rules for Certio Project

## Project Overview
This is a .NET 9.0 web application with AI agents integration. The project uses:
- .NET 9.0 for the main web application
- .NET 8.0 for other projects
- Python 3.11 for AI agents
- SQLite for local development
- Azure SQL Database for production
- Redis for caching

## Code Style and Conventions

### C# (.NET)
- Use C# 12 features where appropriate
- Follow async/await patterns for I/O operations
- Use dependency injection
- Implement proper error handling with try-catch
- Use Entity Framework Core for data access
- Follow Clean Architecture principles

### Python (AI Agents)
- Use type hints
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Use async/await for async operations
- Implement proper error handling
- Use dataclasses for data models
- Follow the existing project structure

## Database Guidelines
- Use Entity Framework migrations for schema changes
- Always use parameterized queries
- Implement proper connection string management
- Use transactions for multi-step operations
- Follow the existing DbContext patterns

## AI Integration
- Use the existing AI service interfaces
- Implement proper error handling for AI API calls
- Use the background service pattern for AI processing
- Follow the existing cost optimization patterns

## File Structure
- Controllers go in Controllers/
- Services go in Services/
- Models go in Domain/ or ViewModels/
- AI agents go in ai_agents/
- Configuration goes in appsettings.json

## Testing
- Write unit tests for business logic
- Use integration tests for API endpoints
- Mock external dependencies
- Follow AAA pattern (Arrange, Act, Assert)

## Security
- Validate all inputs
- Use proper authentication and authorization
- Sanitize data before database operations
- Follow OWASP guidelines

## Performance
- Use async operations where possible
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Optimize database queries
- Use background services for heavy operations